IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`
IMPORT `cda-s10-interpretation`
IMPORT `cda-s5-lawful-excuse`
IMPORT `cda-s1-s3-offences`
IMPORT `cda-fixtures`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, sections 1 to 3: TESTS.
-- Layer 1 tests. Every expected value below was written from the text before the
-- file was run, and is stated in the comment above its assertion, with the reason.
-- A failing assertion here would be a finding, not a value to be edited.

§ `Tests for sections 1 to 3`

§§ `Fixtures: section 1 cases`

`damaging another's property intentionally` MEANS `Section 1 facts` WITH
    `the property` IS `property that another has custody of`
    `the damage` IS `ordinary destruction or damage`
    `the destruction or damage was by fire` IS FALSE
    `intending to destroy or damage any such property` IS TRUE
    `reckless as to whether any such property would be destroyed or damaged` IS FALSE
    `intending to destroy or damage any property` IS TRUE
    `reckless as to whether any property would be destroyed or damaged` IS FALSE
    `intending by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another` IS FALSE
    `reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered` IS FALSE
    `lawful excuse` IS `no lawful excuse`

