    `the user's connection with the property` IS `a person with no connection`
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS TRUE
    `lawful excuse` IS `an honest and justified belief that consent had been given`

`having a thing to damage a wild mushroom that is one's own, knowing the danger` MEANS `Section 3 facts` WITH
    `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS TRUE
    `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS TRUE
    `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS `a wild mushroom that only the accused has custody of`
    `the intended damage` IS `ordinary destruction or damage`
    `the user's connection with the property` IS `a person with no connection`
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS TRUE
    `lawful excuse` IS `no lawful excuse`

`having a thing to alter the contents of a computer only` MEANS `Section 3 facts` WITH
    `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS TRUE
    `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS TRUE
    `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS `property that only the accused has custody of`
    `the intended damage` IS `a modification of the contents of a computer alone`
    `the user's connection with the property` IS `a person with no connection`
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS TRUE
    `lawful excuse` IS `no lawful excuse`

`having a thing to damage another's property with another lawful excuse` MEANS `Section 3 facts` WITH
    `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS TRUE
    `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS TRUE
    `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS `property that another has custody of`
    `the intended damage` IS `ordinary destruction or damage`
    `the user's connection with the property` IS `a person with no connection`
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS FALSE
    `lawful excuse` IS `another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law`

`having a thing to damage one's own property with another lawful excuse, knowing the danger` MEANS `Section 3 facts` WITH
    `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS TRUE
    `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS TRUE
    `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS `property that only the accused has custody of`
    `the intended damage` IS `ordinary destruction or damage`
    `the user's connection with the property` IS `a person with no connection`
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS TRUE
    `lawful excuse` IS `another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law`

`having a thing to do no destruction or damage` MEANS `Section 3 facts` WITH
    `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS TRUE
    `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS TRUE
    `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS `property that another has custody of`
    `the intended damage` IS `no destruction or damage`
    `the user's connection with the property` IS `a person with no connection`
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS FALSE
    `lawful excuse` IS `no lawful excuse`

§§ `Section 1(1) and 1(2)`

-- damaging another's property intentionally. Expected: an offence under s 1(1) is committed -- all the elements of s 1(1) are present; s 1(2)(b) has no state of mind about life.
#ASSERT `a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` `damaging another's property intentionally`

-- damaging another's property intentionally. Expected: an offence under s 1(2) is NOT committed -- all the elements of s 1(1) are present; s 1(2)(b) has no state of mind about life.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` `damaging another's property intentionally`)

-- recklessly damaging another's property. Expected: an offence under s 1(1) is committed -- recklessness is enough under s 1(1).
#ASSERT `a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` `recklessly damaging another's property`

-- recklessly damaging another's property. Expected: an offence under s 1(2) is NOT committed -- recklessness is enough under s 1(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` `recklessly damaging another's property`)

-- damaging another's property with no intent and no recklessness. Expected: an offence under s 1(1) is NOT committed -- neither state of mind in s 1(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` `damaging another's property with no intent and no recklessness`)

-- damaging another's property with no intent and no recklessness. Expected: an offence under s 1(2) is NOT committed -- neither state of mind in s 1(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` `damaging another's property with no intent and no recklessness`)

-- intending to damage property in general but not the property damaged. Expected: an offence under s 1(1) is NOT committed -- s 1(1) asks about 'any such property' (read as property belonging to another: fork F1); s 1(2)(b) has no life element.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` `intending to damage property in general but not the property damaged`)

-- intending to damage property in general but not the property damaged. Expected: an offence under s 1(2) is NOT committed -- s 1(1) asks about 'any such property' (read as property belonging to another: fork F1); s 1(2)(b) has no life element.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` `intending to damage property in general but not the property damaged`)

-- endangering life with no destruction or damage. Expected: an offence under s 1(1) is NOT committed -- no destruction or damage, so neither s 1(1) nor s 1(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` `endangering life with no destruction or damage`)

-- endangering life with no destruction or damage. Expected: an offence under s 1(2) is NOT committed -- no destruction or damage, so neither s 1(1) nor s 1(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` `endangering life with no destruction or damage`)

-- damaging only one's own property, intentionally. Expected: an offence under s 1(1) is NOT committed -- s 1(1) needs property belonging to another; s 1(2)(b) has no life element.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` `damaging only one's own property, intentionally`)

-- damaging only one's own property, intentionally. Expected: an offence under s 1(2) is NOT committed -- s 1(1) needs property belonging to another; s 1(2)(b) has no life element.
